  if(v===1)return statements('Ignore friction and the weight of the pulleys. Evaluate these statements about simple machines.',[['A single fixed pulley changes the direction of the effort.',true],['A single movable pulley lets you lift a load by pulling less rope.',false],['A ramp reduces the force needed but increases the distance moved.',true]],'Machines trade force for distance; they never give out extra energy.',['A movable pulley halves both the effort and the rope you must pull.','A fixed pulley halves the effort because the rope goes over a wheel.'],['A movable pulley halves the effort but doubles the rope pulled.','Less force over more distance does the same job.']);
